<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danilo I, Metropolitan of Cetinje</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1670–<a href="/years/1735">1735</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Danilo Šćepčević</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Danilo I was Metropolitan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetinje">Cetinje</a> from 1697 and founder of the Petrović-Njegoš dynasty, which held the prince-bishopric of Montenegro by succession from uncle to nephew. He led the Montenegrin clans against Ottoman control, and in 1711 allied Montenegro with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, beginning a lasting Russian connection. He died in 1735.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danilo-i-metropolitan-of-cetinje.jpg" alt="Danilo I, Metropolitan of Cetinje" width="320" height="524" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Illustrator of Gorski vijenac · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Danilo_%C5%A0%C4%8Dep%C4%87evi%C4%87,_The_Mountain_Wreath.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
